  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and security enhancements. Key details include: \n\n1. **Launch & Leadership**: Initially introduced with a kick-off in June/July 2023, led by Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole, with a phase one budget of $500,000.\n2. **Team Expansion**: The team has expanded multiple times, adding members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing (e.g., Mike Chen, Lisa Ray, and five new members in September).\n3. **Phases & Development**: The project moved from design to a development phase led by Omar Jensen.\n4. **Security & Compliance**: Security protocols were updated (MFA, encryption) effective January next year. The compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000.\n5. **Training**: A training budget of $15,000 was approved for coding teams and project managers.\n6. **Partnerships**: Discussions are underway with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology."
